Register cleanup immediately after creating the handle using `addTearDown`, so it runs even if an assertion fails:

```dart
testWidgets('accessibility', (tester) async {
  final handle = tester.ensureSemantics();
  addTearDown(handle.dispose);

  await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
  await expectLater(
    tester,
    meetsGuideline(androidTapTargetGuideline),
  );
});
```

Remove the trailing `handle.dispose()`. If the test doesn’t need an additional handle, remove both handle-related lines: `testWidgets` enables semantics and cleans up its own handle automatically.
